## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical debugging of a real-world programmable fabric where data-plane and control-plane interactions directly impact latency. Candidates must correlate low-level telemetry with high-level policy changes to isolate root causes and apply targeted mitigations.

## Key Concepts

- XDP/eBPF data-plane behavior under peak load
- ECMP/hash-based load balancing and collision dynamics
- SDN controller churn and policy stability requirements
- NIC offload pacing and interrupt coalescence interactions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-diagnostic script outline
async function collectDiagnostics() {
  const [bpfStats, hashStats, sdnLogs, nicStats] = await Promise.all([
    getBpfMapStats(),
    getFlowHashDistribution(),
    getSdnPolicyChanges(),
    getNicOffloadMetrics()
  ]);

  return correlateLatencyWithMetrics(bpfStats, hashStats, sdnLogs, nicStats);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical, measurable diagnostics for cross-region latency without code changes, focusing on network-layer factors and real-world tooling. It emphasizes data collection, hypothesis-driven testing, and concrete mitigations across DNS, CDN, and edge routing.

## Key Concepts
- Anycast and IXP ECMP behavior under load
- DNS latency vs HTTP latency as diagnostic signals
- TLS SNI routing at CDNs and edge caches
- CDN origin fetch queuing and caching strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple latency data parser (conceptual)
const fs = require('fs');
const rows = fs.readFileSync('latency.csv','utf8').trim().split('\n');
rows.slice(1).forEach(r => {
  const [region, dns, http] = r.split(',');
  console.log(region, parseFloat(dns), parseFloat(http));
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
